Skeleton3D: update dirty bone poses in one pass, not one per root bone.

_force_update_all_bone_transforms() called _force_update_bone_children_transforms()
once per parentless bone, but that function walks the whole nested set whatever
bone it's given. A skeleton with several roots (WoW models have two to four) walked
every bone that many times, and recomputed every global rest that many times when
rests were dirty. One walk does the same work.

Upstream: not proposed yet. Drop when an equivalent change is in the Godot we pin.

diff --git a/scene/3d/skeleton_3d.cpp b/scene/3d/skeleton_3d.cpp
index f5bca4e..3568ecb 100644
--- a/scene/3d/skeleton_3d.cpp
+++ b/scene/3d/skeleton_3d.cpp
@@ -1072,8 +1072,10 @@ void Skeleton3D::force_update_all_bone_transforms() {
 
 void Skeleton3D::_force_update_all_bone_transforms() const {
 	_update_process_order();
-	for (int i = 0; i < parentless_bones.size(); i++) {
-		_force_update_bone_children_transforms(parentless_bones[i]);
+	// One pass over the nested set updates every dirty bone, whichever root it hangs from,
+	// so it isn't repeated per parentless bone.
+	if (!parentless_bones.is_empty()) {
+		_force_update_bone_children_transforms(parentless_bones[0]);
 	}
 	if (rest_dirty) {
 		rest_dirty = false;
